WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.280
Superman is an American icon, and while the
character is criticized for not being as edgy

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.260
as some of his super-colleagues, not just
anyone can play him.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.660
For truth, justice, and the Hollywood way,
here are our thoughts on the best and worst

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.580
choices for actors to replace Henry Cavill
as Superman.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.880
Best: Matt Bomer

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.780
White Collar's Matt Bomer was considered an
early candidate for Man of Steel, and he actually

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.240
voiced the alien superhero that year in Superman:
Unbound.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.779
Before that, Bomer was cast as Superman before
Brandon Routh in what eventually became Superman

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:32.280
Returns.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.500
According to HuffPost, the same year Bomer
publicly came out as gay at an awards ceremony,

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.260
author Jackie Collins claimed that he was
ousted from the role because of it.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.140
Undoubtedly, Bomer has the looks and the acting
chops to play Superman.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.360
Plus, he's already been cast as Superman — twice!

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.600
Worst: Nicolas Cage

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.310
Believe it or not, a growing number of people
want Nicolas Cage to get another shot at the

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:57.180
role of the Last Son of Krypton.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:03.120
Cage was famously cast in Tim Burton's Superman
Lives, which was never finished because, well,

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.120
sometimes the universe is kind.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.060
Let's be honest.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.690
Cage is too old, Warner Brothers probably
wants people to actually go see their new

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:15.920
Superman movies, and — unless they're planning
a nontraditional, dystopian Superman film

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.220
— Superman is not insane.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.460
Best: Armie Hammer

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.360
One of the names that's coming up more than
others is Cavill's Man from U.N.C.L.E.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.580
co-star Armie Hammer.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.880
He was cast as Batman in George Miller's unrealized
Justice League: Mortal, and according to The

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.060
Hollywood Reporter's blog Heat Vision, he
was also one of the final contenders for Man

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.300
of Steel's Superman role before it went to
Cavill.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.080
Hammer would be a perfect fit.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.460
He's got the height.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:41.220
He's got the physique.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:46.220
And as proven by the well-deserved praise
for his work in 2017's Call Me by Your Name,

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.480
he's got the talent.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.800
Worst: John Krasinski

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.700
Even though John Krasinski isn't at the top
of a lot of lists to replace Cavill, Mark

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.000
Hughes of Forbes thinks he's the perfect choice.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:02.260
Perhaps it's the product of typecasting, but
it's difficult to imagine Krasinski as Superman.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:07.140
Hughes' comparison of Krasinski's character
on The Office to Clark Kent is more than apt,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.080
and that's the problem.

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:12.860
It isn't difficult at all to see Krasinski
as Kent, but it feels almost impossible to

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.420
see him portraying the other half of that
iconic duality.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:21.300
His work in A Quiet Place and Jack Ryan notwithstanding,
Krasinski seems like the guy who plays the

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.280
one who's being saved, not the one who's doing
the saving.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.920
Best: Michael B. Jordan

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:31.180
It didn't take long at all for reports to
surface that Warner Brothers already had a

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.720
frontrunner to replace Cavill as Superman,
and if it pans out, it would arguably be the

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.560
most nontraditional and bold Superman casting
choice to date: Black Panther's Michael B.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.060
Jordan.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.540
Continuously proving himself to be a stellar
actor with huge range, Jordan's one of the

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.180
premiere reasons Black Panther is an Oscar
contender.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.740
And as anyone who's had to hear their partner
talk about Jordan going shirtless can attest,

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:54.060
we know he's got the physique.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.560
Worst: Dwayne Johnson

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.319
The Rock's name is popping up as a potential
candidate for obvious reasons — he sells

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.820
tickets, he's got the body for it, and as
USA Today said,

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.960
"He is Superman, after all."

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.940
However, Dwayne Johnson's commitments to play
the antihero Black Adam would make playing

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.160
Superman in the same narrative difficult.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:20.780
And while Superman is big, muscular, and larger-than-life
just like Johnson, he's also extremely humble,

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.780
and Johnson just may not be that guy.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.130
In fact, if Warner Brothers decided to go
in a different physical direction for Superman's

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:30.440
classic nemesis, Johnson could make a great
Lex Luthor.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.000
He already has the hairdo.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.680
Best: Colin O'Donoghue

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.960
According to The Hollywood Reporter's blog
Heat Vision, Once Upon a Time's Colin O'Donoghue

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:44.760
was one of the actors competing with Cavill
for the role of Superman in 2013's Man of

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:45.260
Steel.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.880
The Irish Post reported that O'Donoghue is
now an early frontrunner to replace him.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.740
O'Donoghue is a good choice, but not a perfect
one.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.960
He certainly has the acting ability and the
looks to play Superman.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.280
But he also has a natural mischievous quality
that you wouldn't ordinarily associate with

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.120
the Man of Steel.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.540
While he would do well in Superman's tights,
you'd almost wonder if he might do better

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.120
in Lex Luthor's office.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.520
Worst: Tyler Hoechlin

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:14.319
DC Comics fans were thrilled when Tyler Hoechlin
appeared as Superman in the second season

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.540
of Supergirl, and many Arrowverse viewers
seem convinced this is the perfect job for

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.040
him.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:23.300
But whether or not you like Hoechlin's take
on the Man of Steel, someone already playing

00:04:23.309 --> 00:04:28.020
Superman in another live-action medium with
a different storyline should not be the guy

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.220
who replaces Cavill.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.580
Having two live-action Supermen played by
two different men is probably confusing enough.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.340
Casting the same guy in both roles?

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:37.160
Forget it.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.640
Best: Henry Golding

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:45.400
Crazy Rich Asians star Henry Golding has emerged
as one of the leading contenders to play Superman

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.320
in any future DCEU projects, and the choice
has promise.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.539
He's a rising star in Hollywood with good
looks and a warm likability — and he's getting

00:04:53.539 --> 00:04:55.159
a lot of attention right now.

00:04:55.159 --> 00:04:58.749
Add to that the fact that Warner Brothers
has been making some very public statements

00:04:58.749 --> 00:05:02.979
recently about their commitment to diversity,
and Golding seems like he has a real shot

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.520
at those blue tights if he wants them.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.840
Worst: Rob Delaney

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:11.270
Comedian Rob Delaney jokingly threw his hat
in the ring for the new Superman the same

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.779
day it was reported that Cavill was out, tweeting,

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.030
"Heard they're in the market for a new Superman.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.740
How sexy are they looking to go?"

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:22.400
While Delaney's Deadpool 2 role certainly
highlighted his flying skills, it's highly

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.380
unlikely that he's a serious contender.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:28.800
Still, it would almost be worth hearing Deadpool
complain about Warner Brothers poaching the

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.550
comedian from his franchise if all it meant
was enduring Delaney as Superman for a film

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:33.899
or two.

